course: dictionary
lesson: 13183
title: Freshness: new, clean and lively
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Freshness is a noun, a thing you can notice and have more or less of. It comes from the word fresh. «The salad had lost its freshness after three days in the fridge.» The limp leaves and dull colour are clues, so freshness means how new and not stale something is.
explain: Freshness also describes air and smells. «The freshness of the sea breeze filled the room.» A breeze cannot be stale. The words sea and breeze, and the feeling of filling a room, point to clean, cool air.
explain: Freshness can mean newness too. «The freshness of her new idea surprised the whole class.» Nothing here is food or air. Check by swapping in the meaning: the new idea surprised the class. It still makes sense, so freshness means newness.
explain: Freshness can describe feeling lively and rested. «After a good sleep, Sam had real freshness in his step.» The words after a good sleep are the clue: he is not tired. Always test your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Freshness is a noun: it names a quality, like softness or kindness.
fact: «Freshness» means being newly made, picked or caught, so food is not old or stale.
fact: «Freshness» can also mean clean, cool air or a clean smell, like mint.
fact: «Freshness» can mean newness and originality, like «the freshness of a new idea».
fact: Cooks and shoppers check freshness by looking at the date and smelling the food.
exercise: «The fish was caught at dawn and sold by noon, so it had great freshness.» What does freshness mean here? | Covered in old smells | *Newly caught, not stale | Sold at a low price | Very cold and wet
exercise: «Open the window and enjoy the freshness of the morning air.» What does freshness mean in this sentence? | Loud noise | A stale smell from the kitchen | Heavy rain | *Clean, cool air
exercise: Maya says: «My new idea has real freshness.» What does she mean? | *Her idea is new and original | Her idea is old and boring | Her idea is written in a jar | Her idea is too big to think about
test: «After a long rest, Sam felt full of freshness.» What does freshness mean here? | *Lively and rested, not tired | Very quiet and shy | Hungry for lunch | Covered in dust
test: A toothpaste label says «Sealed for freshness». Why is the packet sealed? | To show the price | *To keep the toothpaste clean and new | To make the toothpaste heavier to carry | To stop anyone from using it
exam: What does «the freshness of the morning» most likely mean? | A loud argument | A bright red sunset | A long, tiring walk | *Clean, cool, pleasant air
